Why the exception: this application exists partly as a worked example of four
Apache-2.0 libraries — bond, external_service, errata and wait_for_it. The
documentation under docs/, and the code excerpts within it, are meant to be
copied into other projects, including proprietary ones. Placing them under the
AGPL would defeat the purpose of writing them.

The application source itself is AGPL-3.0. Section 13 of that license is the
reason for choosing it over the GPL: running a modified version as a network
service counts as conveying it, so anyone offering a modified OnePlaylist over a
network must offer its users the corresponding source. The plain GPL would not
require that, since serving software over a network is not distribution.
